'' A POINTER 'operator cast' REACHES A POINTER OF THE SAME SIZE, as fbc picks it (structpick.tiko
'' PtrCastScore). 'zstring ptr' into 'byte ptr' and 'ubyte ptr', 'wstring ptr' into 'short ptr' and
'' 'ushort ptr', 'byte ptr' and 'ubyte ptr' into 'zstring ptr', 'long ptr' into 'ulong ptr',
'' 'integer ptr' into 'longint ptr' -- on a single procedure, in an overload set where the pair is
'' not ranked first in the parameter's row, from an initialiser and an assignment. Among two casts
'' the closer pointee wins over another size, and 'any ptr' over a same-size one. tiko knew only
'' 'exact or any ptr': every one of these was TKO0698, or TKO0994 in a set. Output is fbc-modern's.
'' A tie inside ONE overload of a set only takes that overload out (the last two lines).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/ptrcast-samesize.bas -o tests/codegen/ptrcastsamesize.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/ptrcastsamesize.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [zs] sb 65
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [zs] su66
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [ws] sh 67
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [ws] sw68
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [by] sz AB
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [ub] sz AB
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [lo] sl4294967291
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [in] sq 77
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [zs] ob 65 1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [by] oz AB 1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [ws] os 67 1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [zs] sb 65
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [an] sb 65
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [zs] pu65
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [by] pz AB
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [zs] tz 2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [by] tb 2
